WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:10.340
cudaMalloc reserves GPU storage for d_x and d_y. cudaMemcpy copies sizeof(x) bytes from CPU array x to d_x.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:17.105
The later kernel launch passes n elements, and a device-to-host copy fills CPU array y before it is printed.

00:00:18.605 --> 00:00:19.530
Allocate.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.620
Reserve separate GPU input and output storage.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:23.825
Copy input.

00:00:23.825 --> 00:00:27.090
Move x from CPU memory to d_x.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.535
Run and read back.

00:00:28.535 --> 00:00:32.095
Write d_y, then copy its values to y.

00:00:33.595 --> 00:00:36.055
CPU arrays live in system RAM.

00:00:36.055 --> 00:00:39.145
Device arrays live in GPU device memory.

00:00:39.145 --> 00:00:45.185
Allocation reserves storage; copying moves values, and the SM executes the calculation.
